{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:AppendixStandardModel.SmGaugeTruncation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"AppendixStandardModel.SmGaugeTruncation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.UnitaryGroup","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Complex.Basic"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.not_standardModelTruncation_of_subsingleton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.not_standardModelTruncation_of_subsingleton","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-standard-model/sm-gauge-truncation.lean#L62-L75","doc":"The conjecture class has falsifiable content: it fails for any\nsubsingleton `G`, because the `U(1)` factor already contains the\nnontrivial element `-1` and an injective homomorphism cannot\nidentify it with the identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.negOneU1_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.negOneU1_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-standard-model/sm-gauge-truncation.lean#L57-L60","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.negOneU1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.negOneU1","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-standard-model/sm-gauge-truncation.lean#L52-L55","doc":"`-1` is a unitary scalar: the nontrivial element of `U(1)`\nwitnessing that the Standard-Model product group is nontrivial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.StandardModelTruncation.sm_embeds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.StandardModelTruncation.sm_embeds","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-standard-model/sm-gauge-truncation.lean#L46-L46","doc":"`SU(3) × SU(2) × U(1)` embeds in `G`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.StandardModelTruncation.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.StandardModelTruncation.mk","kind":"ctor","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-standard-model/sm-gauge-truncation.lean#L44-L44","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.StandardModelTruncation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.StandardModelTruncation","kind":"class","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-standard-model/sm-gauge-truncation.lean#L35-L50","doc":"**Conjecture (Standard-Model truncation).** The group `G`\n(intended: the archimedean truncation of the QOU gauge symmetry)\ncontains an embedded copy of `SU(3) × SU(2) × U(1)`: there is an\ninjective group homomorphism from the product into `G`.\n\nFalsifiable content: the field fails for any `G` too small or too\ncommutative to host the product (e.g. any abelian `G`, since\n`SU(3)` is non-abelian and homomorphic images of non-abelian simple\ncompact groups in abelian groups kill them, breaking injectivity). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:sm-gauge-truncation","label":"conj:sm-gauge-truncation","md":"quantum-observable-universe/appendix-standard-model/sm-gauge-truncation.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}